            <ArticleTitle>Myxoid neurothekeoma--a painful case in a less common location.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myxoid neurothekeoma is a rare benign asymptomatic tumor of the skin. Most tumors are located on the head, shoulders and arms. We present a 19-year-old female patient with a relapsing tumor of this type in a less common localization, i.e., lower trunk, and with painful sensations under mechanical pressure. Wide excision surgery led to complete remission.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
